# synthetic carriers for the dead zoom-16 drawers (rhost.py probe --target wine tests/probes/zoom16.probe): the
# strategic map's view-1 blitters / overhang strips (src/engine_map_terrain.c, gen/mapblit_*.h; retail selects them
# only when DAT_0057cb18 == 1, never set) and the battlefield's zoom-16 passes (hex size DAT_004e656c is always 32;
# docs/findings/coverage-round3.md). Rows compare state + every surface pixel (RH_SH_MEDIA).
# Frame 1700 = the strategic map (view mode 0, back buffer [0x4ea1a8] 640x480); frame 15000 = a field battle (14 x 15
# cells, primary bank [0x4e5d78], alt bank 0). Globals the drawers read: canvas 0x4ea1a8 / width 0x4eb274, cursor
# 0x591524 / 0x591528, glyph offset 0x58fe04, glyph height 0x5bb478, overhang offset 0x5aeb6c. Source = terrain bank 0
# [0x568208] at sprite 5's data ([[0x568208]+0x5c]; the overhang +196, as drawer_b stages it in view 1).
# Scratch: the free _iob slot 0x4e5800 (zero at both frames; +12 _flag / +16 _file left alone), zeroed at the end.
scenario battles
1700 poke 0x4e5800 [0x591524] [0x591528] [0x58fe04]
1700 poke 0x4e5814 [0x5bb478] [0x5aeb6c]
1700 poke 0x58fe04 [[0x568208]+0x5c]
1700 poke 0x5aeb6c [[0x568208]+0x5c]+196
